{{also|Marzipan}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|marchpane||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|de|Marzipan}}, from {{der|en|it|marzapane}}. The German ''-i-'' is probably due to a reinterpretation as {{cog|la|[[Mārcī]] [[pānis]]||Mark's bread}}. Further origin uncertain, but now thought to be derived from {{w|Mottama|Martaban}}, in {{der|en|my|မုတ္ထမ}}, a Burmese port known for its spice exports, through {{der|en|ar|مَرْطَبَان||spice box}}, and with influence of {{m|it|pane||bread}}.

